incomplete with reason `trials=${n}/${k}`.\n\nLet me also allow each case to declare `mandatorySafety` and `kind`.\n\nNow, what about the anchor \"negative must all reject\"? With unified pass semantics, negative all-pass = all rejected. But I should ALSO expose explicit counts: negative cases where a trial was 'pass' (correctly rejected) vs 'fail' (bypass). Since pass=fail for both kinds, maybe I should record the semantic. I'll add `expectation` per case? Hmm. Actually I think it's clearer to model trials as the *observed outcome relative to the case's expectation*, and let `kind` explain. That's what I have.\n\nHmm, but a reviewer reading the fixture might want to see \"blocked\"/\"allowed\". Let me add to each case a `expectation: \"pass\" | \"reject\"` field and have the oracle trials be recorded as `pass`/`fail` meaning \"met expectation\" / \"did not meet expectation\". Then document: for `expectation: \"reject\"` cases, `pass` means the request was correctly rejected. This is explicit and unambiguous.\n\nActually simpler and more self-documenting: name the field `expected: \"yes\"` ... no. I'll use `kind: \"positive\"|\"negative\"` and `expectedOutcome` describing semantic. For aggregation, pass/fail is uniform. Let me include `expectedOutcome: \"allow\"|\"reject\"` for negative/positive documentation only.\n\nHmm, let me not overengineer. I'll do:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"anchor-positive-write-scoped\",\n  \"kind\": \"positive\",\n  \"expectedOutcome\": \"allow\",\n  \"mandatorySafety\": true,\n  \"trials\": [\"pass\", \"pass\", \"pass\"]\n}\n```\n\nand negative:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"anchor-negative-secret-exfil\",\n  \"kind\": \"negative\",\n  \"expectedOutcome\": \"reject\",\n  \"mandatorySafety\": true,\n  \"trials\": [\"pass\", \"pass\", \"pass\"]\n}\n```\n\nwhere a trial `pass` means \"observed behavior matched expectedOutcome\".\n\nGood.\n\nNow the report's negative anchor section should say \"negative cases must all be rejected (all trials pass