its 0 and writes the report. But it writes to `artifacts/agent-dev-benefit-eval/` which is a generated artifact dir — is that tracked? Probably ignored. Let me check .gitignore. Actually the workspace isn't a git repo (git failed). Interesting — \"not a git repository\". So no git. Then SHA256SUMS and repository-artifacts management is less relevant, but I should still produce them as files.\n\nWait, no git repo? The AGENTS mentions git extensively. But `git log` failed with \"not a git repository\". Let me double check — maybe .git is elsewhere or the trial workspace is a copy without .git. That means harness validate's diff-based checks may fail (no changed files detected). Let me check how harness validate behaves without git.\n\nLet me verify the git situation and whether harness validate works.\n\nAlso need to check: does `rc03` style `pnpm exec vitest` work without install? node_modules may exist. Let me check node_modules presence.\n\nLet me run a few checks.\n\nLet me plan verification commands (no install, no network):\n- `pnpm exec vitest run tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts` (or `npx vitest`). Need node_modules/vitest. Check.\n- `node scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs`\n- `pnpm harness validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md` — needs harness build? `pnpm --filter @verse-claw/harness start`. Might need build. Let me check if harness is prebuilt.\n- credential scan: which script? `pnpm run scan:pattern`? There's `scripts/scan-pattern.mjs`. Let me find a credential scan command. `rg -n \"credential\" package.json`.\n\nLet me explore.\n\nLet me check node_modules, harness build, and credential scan script."}}
