{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"node --version 2>&1; pnpm --version 2>&1; Write-Output '=== harness/package.json ==='; Get-Content harness/package.json -Raw; Write-Output '=== harness/src/cli.mjs head ==='; Get-Content harness/src/cli.mjs -TotalCount 60\"","aggregated_output":"v24.22.1\r\n11.2.2\n=== harness/package.json ===\r\n{\n  \"name\": \"@verse-claw/harness\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"verse-claw-harness\": \"./src/cli.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node src/cli.mjs\"\n  }\n}\n\r\n=== harness/src/cli.mjs head ===\r\n#!/usr/bin/env node\r\nimport process from 'node:process';\r\nimport { buildContext, formatContext } from './context.mjs';\r\nimport { getChangedFiles, resolveDefaultDiffBase, resolveDiffBase } from './git.mjs';\r\nimport { PROFILES, selectSteps } from './profiles.mjs';\r\nimport { writeReport } from './report.mjs';\r\nimport { runStep } from './runner.mjs';\r\nimport {\r\n  isGatewayBackendCommunicationTask,\r\n  isPluginLifecycleTask,\r\n  loadGuideSpecs,\r\n  loadLayerSpecs,\r\n  loadRuleSpecs,\r\n  loadScenarioSpecs,\r\n  loadSpec,\r\n  toArray,\r\n} from './specs.mjs';\r\nimport {\r\n  scanBackendCommunicationBoundary,\r\n  touchesCommunicationPath,\r\n  classifyChangedPathOwnership,\r\n  validateChangedPathOwnership,\r\n  validateGatewayTaskSpec,\r\n  validatePluginLifecycleTaskSpec,\r\n  validateSpecPortability,\r\n} from './rules.mjs';\r\n\r\nfunction parseArgs(argv) {\r\n  const args = { _: [] };\r\n  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {\r\n    const arg = argv[i];\r\n    if (arg === '--') continue;\r\n    if (!arg.startsWith('--')) {\r\n      args._.push(arg);\r\n      continue;\r\n    }\r\n    const key = arg.slice(2);\r\n    const next = argv[i + 1];\r\n    if (!next || next.startsWith('--')) {\r\n      args[key] = true;\r\n      continue;\r\n    }\r\n    args[key] = next;\r\n    i += 1;\r\n  }\r\n  return args;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction printUsage() {\r\n  console.log([\r\n    'Usage:',\r\n    '  pnpm harness list',\r\n    '  pnpm harness validate --spec <path> [--since origin/main] [--no-diff]',\r\n    '  pnpm harness explain --spec <path> [--since origin/main]',\r\n    '  pnpm harness context --spec <path> [--json]',\r\n    '  pnpm harness run --spec <path> [--since origin/main] [--dry-run] [--continue-on-error]',\r\n  ].join('\\n'));\r\n}\r\n\r\nasync function findScenario(id) {\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"reasoning","text":"Harness CLI can run with pure node (no deps). Let me verify harness validate and dry-run works on the existing spec to know the flow. But there's no git, so diff-based validation may fail. Let me try `pnpm harness list`. Actually pnpm harness requires the @verse-claw/harness workspace filter which needs pnpm install maybe. But harness start is just `node src/cli.mjs`, and the cli only uses node builtins. So I can run `node harness/src/cli.mjs list`.\n\nLet me test it. Also I can run the benefit eval script (pure node, uses node builtins only).\n\nLet me plan the implementation now. Let me check what the existing agent-dev-benefit-eval report looks like and check if there's an artifacts dir.\n\nLet me now think about the actual deliverable design.\n\nThe task: \"E01 在 Agent Dev benefit 报告里加入确定性的 pass^k、逐 trial 成功率、flake 与正反锚点聚合；缺失/超时/崩溃/skip 显式保留，pass^k 不与 pass@k 混用，不改产品默认或产品锁，不宣称真实模型泛化。\"\n\nTarget scope files:\n- scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs (modify: add reliability aggregation section)\n- scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs (new: pure functions)\n- scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.d.mts (new: typing surface)\n- shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json (new: deterministic fixture with k=3, minCases>=20, flake threshold pre-registered)\n- tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts (new)\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md (new task spec)\n- harness/specs/rules/reliability-aggregation-boundary.md (new rule)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md (new report)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-acceptance.json (new)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/E01-SHA256SUMS (new)\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. Reuse existing agent-dev benefit report + scenario registry; no new metrics platform; k, minCases, flake threshold pre-registered in fixture.\n2. pass^k (fraction of complete cases passing all k trials) vs pass@k (at least one pass) separate; missing/timeout/crash/skip cases counted as incomplete, excluded from denominator and retained in report.\n3. flake = fraction of cases that failed first trial then succeeded on fixed rerun; keep first failure; retry success doesn't erase original gate failure; safety-must-test 0 skip/0 flake.\n4. positive/negative anchors: positive must all pass, negative must all reject; violation => gate=fail.\n5. complete case count below design gate (k=3, >=20) => gate=insufficient-sample; never pass small sample as PASS.\n6. Report gives raw denominator, pass^k, pass@k, flake, missing, gate, reason; fixture is deterministic oracle and explicitly labeled; no claiming real provider/human/generalization.\n7. Clean-candidate fast gate (targeted unit, runtime/core types, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run) passes, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS re-readable; README four languages reviewed: this packet only changes internal eval report, no user-visible interface/config change, so README unchanged, conclusion in acceptance record.\n8. No product defaults, product locks, or approval semantics changed; no new scheduled automation.\n\nSo I need to implement reliability-aggregation logic in scripts/lib, wire it into agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs, and create fixture + test + spec + rule + docs.\n\nLet me check if the domain is TS-typed. The lib is .mjs with .d.mts typing surface. The unit test imports from scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs.\n\nLet me look at one existing lib+test to match conventions (e.g., system-maturity-* or tf0009). Let me look at a test that imports a lib module with node env.\n\nLet me look at scripts/lib/tf0009-canary-readiness.mjs + d.mts and its test.\n\nAlso I should check how `agent-dev-benefit-eval` is tested — is there a unit test for it? Let me search.\n\nLet me check harness validate require diff and how it handles no-git. Let me just run node harness/src/cli.mjs list.\n\nLet me batch these explorations."}}
