≤1%\" — so with ≥20 cases but only 14 non-security, 1 flake = 7% > 1% → fail. So a passing oracle must have 0 flake, OR denominator ≥ 100. That's impractical. \n\nHmm wait, maybe flake rate denominator is all complete cases (20), 1/20 = 5% still > 1%. So any flake fails at n=20.\n\nSo: the oracle fixture for a healthy PASS must have ZERO flake. But then how to demonstrate \"flake retained\"? The report still computes flake and lists flakeCases (empty for oracle). The unit tests construct flake variants.\n\nBut acceptance says \"flake = ... 保留首次失败，重试成功不洗掉原门失败\" — meaning the mechanism must exist and be tested. I'll include a flake demonstration in the unit test (constructed input) and possibly a second fixture variant. Hmm, but the requirement \"缺失/超时/崩溃/skip 显式保留\" wants the oracle to include incomplete cases retained while still passing. Incomplete cases don't count against flake denominator... wait, do incomplete cases get excluded from BOTH pass^k denominator AND flake denominator? Yes, incomplete excluded from complete cases. So flake denominator = complete non-security cases = 20 - securityComplete. If security complete = 6, non-sec = 14; 1 flake → 7.1% fail.\n\nSo to have flake 0 in the pass oracle. But maybe I can make the oracle have a larger denominator: 100 cases? \">=20\". Could have 25 complete, 6 security, 19 non-security; 1 flake = 5.26% still >1%.\n\nSo realistically the oracle needs 0 flake to pass. But wait — maybe flake is measured and the gate uses it, but the threshold applies only if there ARE flake cases; and \"同时报告样本不足\" — report insufficient sample for flake. Actually the design says \"非安全flake≤1%，同时报告样本不足\". Meaning: if sample insufficient to judge flake rate, report insufficient rather than fail. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider the gate. Perhaps flake shouldn't hard-fail the whole gate when sample is small; instead it contributes. But acceptance criterion 5 says gate=insufficient-sample only when complete case count < minCases. And criterion 3 says flake retention + security 0 skip/0 flake.\n\nI think the safest, defensible interpretation: \n- The overall gate fails on: safety/anchor violations, or non-security flake rate strictly greater than threshold. \n- For the committed deterministic oracle to PASS, it must have zero non-security flake.\n\nTo still \"保留缺失/超时/崩溃/skip\" and demonstrate flake-handling, I'll:\n- Include incomplete cases (timeout + skip, non-security) retained in oracle → excluded from denominators, gate still pass.\n- Include flake demonstration ONLY in unit-test variants (constructed), plus record in the report that flake=0 for the oracle.\n\nHmm, but the acceptance says the report \"同时给出 ... flake、缺失 ...\". It gives flake value 0 — fine.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider: maybe include a flake case in the oracle AND make the oracle gate = 'fail'? But then \"clean candidate fast 门通过\" etc. The E01 acceptance report decision would be... Hmm. The oracle is meant to be a deterministic PASS demonstrating the aggregation works. If it includes a flake it fails.\n\nAlternative: define flakeRate denominator as the raw complete-case count (20). 1/20 = 5% still >1%.\n\nAlternatively maybe threshold nonSecurityFlakeRateMax should be interpreted per the design's 1%, and the oracle simply has 0 flake. That's fine and honest. The \"保留首次失败\" behavior is verified by unit tests using constructed inputs.\n\nBut hmm — \"缺失/超时/崩溃/skip 显式保留\" wants to show retention. I can include a timeout and a skip and a crash and a missing case in the oracle (4 incomplete) — all non-security, so gate stays pass, and they're retained in `incompleteCases`. Good. That demonstrates retention.\n\nAnd flake: I'll add a NON-gate-affecting demonstration? No. Let me instead include a flake case but ALSO ensure the gate reports it. If gate fails due to flake, the oracle isn't a clean PASS. Hmm.\n\nLet me re-read the acceptance criteria #3 more carefully: \"flake = 首次 trial 失败、后续固定重跑成功的 case 比例；保留首次失败，重试成功不洗掉原门失败；安全必测项 0 skip/0 